/ A resume goes on in a sub app of the resuming actor, and a sub app takes in its maker's bindings at birth: a binding
/ this app made after the save — so the snapshot holds none — fires in the resumed run. Plan saves the run; this goal
/ then binds Log before each goal and resumes. The resumed run goes on through this goal too, from the step after
/ `call Plan`: the marker sends it to Resumed, and Log, taken in from this app, runs before Resumed starts and notes it.
Start
- call Plan
- if file 'workspace/resumed.marker' exists
    - call Resumed
    - end goal
- write "here" to file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- before each goal, call Log
- resume %run%
- read file 'workspace/seen.txt', write to %seen%
- assert %seen% equals "Resumed"
- delete file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- delete file 'workspace/seen.txt'

/ The run that is saved, with no binding made yet.
Plan
- save snapshot, write to %run%

/ The bound call: notes the goal that is starting.
Log
- set %logged% = %!event!item.name%

/ The resumed run's end: what Log noted, written where the asker reads it.
Resumed
- write "%logged%" to file 'workspace/seen.txt'
